{%- comment -%}
  LOOK is headless. look.ind.in (Vercel) is the real storefront; this Shopify theme
  exists only so Shopify can host checkout on shop.look.ind.in, which is the store's
  primary domain. Two consequences we are fixing here:

    1. Shopify redirects look-10300.myshopify.com -> shop.look.ind.in, so the
       near-empty default theme is publicly reachable on a branded URL.
    2. Shopify's own order-confirmation and abandoned-cart emails link to the
       primary domain, so "continue shopping" lands customers in that bare theme.

  INSTALL — two steps, and step 2 is a single line:

    1. Edit code -> Snippets -> Add a new snippet, name it `headless-redirect`,
       replace the placeholder contents with this whole file, Save.
    2. Edit code -> layout/theme.liquid. Find the line that reads
       {{ content_for_header }} and add this on the line directly BELOW it:

           {% render 'headless-redirect' %}

       Do not remove or move {{ content_for_header }} — Shopify refuses to save
       theme.liquid without it in the head section, which is the FileSaveError
       you get if it goes missing.

  Why this is safe:
    - Checkout and the order status page are NOT theme-rendered on the Basic plan,
      so nothing here can touch the checkout flow.
    - The Storefront API is not theme-rendered either, so the headless site is
      completely unaffected.
    - request.design_mode is true inside the theme editor, so the editor keeps working.
    - password / captcha / gift_card pages are passed through untouched: redirecting
      them would lock out a password-protected store or hide a gift card code.

  Path mapping matches src/App.tsx. Shopify product handles are our /shop/:slug
  values (ProductDetail calls getProductByHandle(slug)), so product links survive.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign storefront = 'https://look.ind.in' -%}
{%- assign passthrough = 'password,captcha,gift_card' | split: ',' -%}

{%- unless request.design_mode or passthrough contains request.page_type -%}
  {%- case request.page_type -%}
    {%- when 'product' -%}
      {%- assign target = storefront | append: '/shop/' | append: product.handle -%}
    {%- when 'cart' -%}
      {%- assign target = storefront | append: '/cart' -%}
    {%- when 'collection' or 'list-collections' or 'search' -%}
      {%- assign target = storefront | append: '/shop' -%}
    {%- when 'policy' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Match on a substring of request.path rather than splitting it. An exact
        match on the last path segment is brittle: locale prefixes, trailing
        slashes and Shopify's own handle variations all break it, and the failure
        is silent (everything falls through to the homepage).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if request.path contains 'refund' -%}
        {%- assign target = storefront | append: '/returns' -%}
      {%- elsif request.path contains 'shipping' -%}
        {%- assign target = storefront | append: '/shipping' -%}
      {%- elsif request.path contains 'privacy' -%}
        {%- assign target = storefront | append: '/privacy' -%}
      {%- elsif request.path contains 'terms' -%}
        {%- assign target = storefront | append: '/terms' -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign target = storefront | append: '/' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign target = storefront | append: '/' -%}
  {%- endcase -%}

  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ target }}">
  <script>window.location.replace({{ target | json }});</script>
{%- endunless -%}
